                <pb facs="0878" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1428: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-14T09:00:00-04:00">October 14, 1931—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>104. My telegram No. 103, October 10, 2 p.m. The reply to the Legation’s note
                    presented pursuant to instructions to [<hi rendition="#italic">in</hi>] the
                    Department’s telegram No. 39, October 3, noon,<anchor n="96" xml:id="d625-f1"/>
                    states: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In reply I am able to inform you that the delegation of Paraguay will be
                            on the date indicated in Washington, properly instructed for the opening
                            of the meetings”.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wheeler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
